//! FES2014b ocean-tide geopotential coefficients (IERS Conventions 2010, Eq. 6.15) --
//! machine-generated by `derivations/ocean_tide_fes2014.py` from `fes2014b_Cnm-Snm.txt`.
//! Full model to degree/order 100 (no truncation); verbatim file values, the 10^-11 unit is
//! [`SCALE`], applied at use. The runtime evaluation degree is chosen on
//! [`crate::ocean_tide::OceanTide`], not here. Regenerate, never hand-edit.
//!
//! The coefficient body lives in the sibling `ocean_tide_fes2014_table.in` and is included verbatim. Every
//! source-level tool parses each `.rs` module in the tree whole -- `syn`, and through it
//! `cargo-mutants`, plus `rustfmt` and `rust-analyzer` -- and this one table is large enough
//! that it alone took `cargo mutants --list` on this crate from 9.6 s to over twelve minutes
//! without finishing. `include!` hands rustc exactly the same tokens and leaves the module a
//! page long, so the crate can be mutation-tested at all.

// Verbatim FES2014b coefficients: many share the same few significant digits; the model name
// FES2014b reads as camel-case to `doc_markdown`.
#![allow(
    clippy::unreadable_literal,
    clippy::excessive_precision,
    clippy::approx_constant,
    clippy::doc_markdown
)]

use crate::ocean_tide_fes2004::OceanTideWave;

/// FES2014b coefficient scale: file values are in units of 10^-11 (as FES2004; Orekit
/// `FESCnmSnmReader`).
pub const SCALE: f64 = 1.0e-11;

include!("ocean_tide_fes2014_table.in");
